<!-- ===== SECTION 10 ===== -->
<h1>10. Quick Reference Glossary</h1>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th width="30%">Term</th>
    <th>Definition</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Due Sheet</strong></td>
    <td>The Excel file you upload containing all outstanding invoices. Each row = one invoice. This is the "current" list of who owes you money.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Master Contacts</strong></td>
    <td>The Excel file containing dealer company profiles — email addresses, WhatsApp numbers, SMS numbers, and contact person names. Used to know WHERE to send reminders.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Reminder Log</strong></td>
    <td>A record of every reminder that was generated (and possibly sent). Each reminder has a status: pending, sent, or failed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Generation</strong></td>
    <td>The process of creating reminder entries in the system for all eligible invoices. Does not send anything — just prepares the queue.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Dispatch</strong></td>
    <td>The actual sending of reminder messages via Email, WhatsApp, or SMS to dealers.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Bill Age</strong></td>
    <td>Number of days since the invoice was raised (Bill Date → Today).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Overdue Days</strong></td>
    <td>Number of days the payment is past its due date (Due Date → Today). 0 or negative = still current.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Cooldown (5-day rule)</strong></td>
    <td>A minimum 5-day gap enforced between reminders to the same dealer. Prevents spam and maintains professionalism.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Pending</strong></td>
    <td>Reminder generated and waiting to be dispatched (in the queue).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Sent</strong></td>
    <td>Reminder successfully delivered to the dealer via the chosen channel.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Failed</strong></td>
    <td>Reminder could not be delivered — usually because of missing or invalid contact details.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Matched Contact</strong></td>
    <td>The system successfully found the dealer in Master Contacts AND found a valid address (email/phone) for the reminder channel.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Missing Contact</strong></td>
    <td>The dealer exists in the Due Sheet but has no matching row in Master Contacts, OR the Master Contact entry is missing the required email/phone number.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Archived</strong></td>
    <td>Historical data — the last known balance from old reminder logs, shown when the dealer is no longer in the current active Due Sheet.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>No Active Due Sheet</strong></td>
    <td>The dealer has reminder history but their invoices are not present in the currently loaded Due Sheet (paid up, removed, or name mismatch).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Ageing Stage</strong></td>
    <td>Which "bucket" an invoice falls into based on how old it is (e.g., 30-45 Days, 46-60 Days, 60+ Days). Configured in Rules/Settings.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Trigger Rule</strong></td>
    <td>The specific reminder rule (based on bill age in days) that caused a reminder to be generated. Example: "30d Rule" = triggered because the bill is 30+ days old.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Days Elapsed</strong></td>
    <td>How many days have passed since the last reminder was sent to a dealer.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Success Rate</strong></td>
    <td>Percentage of reminders successfully delivered out of all attempted (sent + failed). Pending reminders are excluded.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Failure Rate</strong></td>
    <td>Percentage of reminders that failed out of all attempted. High failure rate = update your Master Contacts.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Total Outstanding</strong></td>
    <td>The sum of all outstanding amounts in the current Due Sheet — total receivables from all dealers combined.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

